      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture of the test. The `test_era_yearDay` method tests `dateYearDay` for the British cutover year 1752 (which only had 355 days due to the 11-day Julian→Gregorian gap) and a modern year. The class is cluttered with many unused data-provider methods. I'll:\n1. Remove all the unused data-provider methods (they are never `@MethodSource`-referenced by the single `@Test` in this file)\n2. Add brief comments explaining the cutover context for each assertion\n3. Remove unused importsThe improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes all unused data-provider methods and imports, extracts the chronology singleton into a named constant, and adds brief comments explaining the cutover context (the 11-day Julian→Gregorian gap in September 1752) for each assertion — making the test's intent immediately clear to any reader."
